Expected elements: present

Backbone present, nothing forbidden. The focus holder is the identity bar's `0xb63616…6359`, wearing a 2px #3b82f6 outline at x81-197 / y17-45.

HYDRATION MOVED NOTHING, and I can prove it rather than assert it. I decoded both PNGs and compared them pixel-for-pixel against `screenshots/debugger__wide__light.png` — the same transaction (`readyTx`, `0xb636167a05b9de55bde67756bdaed6e766d46359`) served from the plain tree. The two 1920x1080 frames differ in 568 pixels of 2,073,600. All 568 are exactly #3b82f6 and all sit inside x81-197 / y17-45, which is precisely the perimeter of a 117x29 box with a 2px stroke (117*29 - 113*25 = 568). `outline` does not participate in flow and nothing in this frame moved. The dark pair gives the identical result: 568px, same bbox, #60a5fa. The MUST-NOT-SHOW is clean.

But the ring does not surround a control. Removing the 2px width and 2px offset leaves an element box of 109x21 at x85-193 / y21-41 — the glyph box, zero padding, no border, no background, no radius. This bar's control band is 27px (chips and divider, y18-44) and its badge is 23px (y20-42). The one element the page calls a button owns the shortest box in the bar and the tallest ring on it (findings 1, 2).

Two claims in the expectation block are false against the build (findings 3, 4).

Fixes: give `.copybtn` the bar's 27px control geometry; correct the block.

Rating: 6/10

